module gunbc.cli_run_workspace_root_scaffold

import std.types { String, Int }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, dissolution_description, unbound_dissolution }


data cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
    decl_name: "workspace_root_from",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_dissolve_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "🟡 dissolve-on: workspace_root_from — runtime workspace-root discovery in HAND-Rust (#6484 .git-ancestor kernel); DISSOLVES WHEN cli_run.rs Chunk F lands (docs/plans/cli-run-reconcile-defork.md → GENERATED workflow host-effect apply) OR ROADMAP 5-dissolve-patches cli_run.rs shrink retires HAND path-dependent root entirely")

// THE CHECKOUT ROOT RECEIVED AT SPAWN, the dissolution the scaffold above names, landed for the
// release-locus population (parent ruling 2026-09-21): the seed reads ONE environment name at one
// site (workspace_root_resolve, consumed by workspace_root and process_workspace_root), treats it as
// the authority when set -- no walk, a typed refusal naming the path and the missing member when it
// holds no dag/ or no tree receipt -- and walks exactly as before when unset. Both unit emitters
// (gunbc.live_deploy.emit: the approval broker's serve unit and the microVM slot unit) set it from
// THIS row, and so does the SEED -- gunbc.release_locus_seed_constants_emit projects both rows into
// release_locus_seed_constants_generated.rs and cli_run.rs consumes them, so there is no second
// authoring of either spelling to drift. The discriminators below name the executed controls. v1 admission (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing): this is SEED GROWTH,
// not a v2 self-host step -- 87 hand-Rust lines on the existing workspace_root_from scaffold, rostered
// as that row's census (cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_loc_delta_net, 12 -> 99) and retired by
// that row's dissolve trigger, not by anything this change adds. Its purpose link is the release
// locus the slot controller runs from; it is admitted as bounded growth on a tracked row, not as
// serving self-hosting.
data gunbc_workspace_root_env_name: String = "GUNBC_WORKSPACE_ROOT"

data release_locus_tree_receipt_name: String = ".gunbc-tree-receipt"

data cli_run_workspace_root_spawn_test_discriminator_authority: String = "spawn_root_is_authority_and_the_walk_is_not_consulted"

data cli_run_workspace_root_spawn_test_discriminator_refusal: String = "spawn_root_without_receipt_refuses_instead_of_walking"

data cli_run_workspace_root_hand_rust_receipt_plan_anchor: String = "docs/plans/cli-run-reconcile-defork.md#interim-workspace-root-scaffold"

// RE-DERIVED FOR THE SPAWN ARM, because the row is bound to `workspace_root_from` at
// WholeDeclaration and this change grows exactly that declaration's hand-Rust. It was 12 -- the
// .git-ancestor kernel alone -- and a row left at 12 while the declaration it binds gained the
// spawn arm would be the parallel-ledger DESIGN section 6 refuses, stating a figure the tree
// contradicts while its only consumer (`... > 0`) cannot see it move.
//
// THE INSTRUMENT, named rather than the count alone (DESIGN section 6): the added non-blank lines
// of this scaffold's hand-Rust in cli_run.rs, excluding its `#[test]` module, re-derive with
//   git diff -w <merge-base>...HEAD -U0 -- src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs \
//     | awk '/^@@/{h=$0} /^\+[^+]/{c[h]++} END{for (k in c) print c[k], k}'
// with -w because re-indentation is not growth. After main's gunbc#11960 made the process root a
// bound (root, basis) pair, the spawn root joins it as its own basis (Spawned) in both the
// panicking resolver and the typed bind, so the report never calls a spawned locus discovered; the
// instrument then reports 87 outside the test module (42 more inside it, excluded on the same
// basis the 12 excluded its own tests). 12 + 87 = 99.
data cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_loc_delta_net: Int = 99

data cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_test_discriminator_git_toplevel: String = "from_subdirectory_matches_git_toplevel"

data cli_run_workspace_root_discovery_test_discriminator_cwd_ascent: String = "refuses_path_outside_git_checkout"

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
    decl_name: "try_anchor_source_root",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_dissolve_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "🟡 dissolve-on: try_anchor_source_root — declared layer/pool-root anchoring in HAND-Rust while dag/compiler is modeled-before-implemented (§6 model-first), so root absence is a legitimate state the walk skips LOUDLY (counted stderr line per root), never a mid-floor panic; CLI-provided roots keep the panicking anchor_source_root contract. DISSOLVES WHEN cli_run.rs Chunk F lands (docs/plans/cli-run-reconcile-defork.md → the roots walk is GENERATED and absence becomes a typed, located, counted diagnostic at the roster layer) OR ROADMAP 5-dissolve-patches cli_run.rs shrink retires HAND path handling entirely")

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_receipt_plan_anchor: String = "docs/plans/cli-run-reconcile-defork.md#interim-workspace-root-scaffold"

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_loc_delta_net: Int = 43

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_test_discriminator_present_root: String = "try_anchor_source_root_resolves_declared_present_root"

data cli_run_source_root_anchor_test_discriminator_absent_root: String = "try_anchor_source_root_skips_declared_absent_root"

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
    decl_name: "bind_process_workspace_root",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_dissolve_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "🟡 dissolve-on: bind_process_workspace_root — the two-rule workspace-root SELECTION (discovery is the incumbent authority; where no checkout exists the request names the base, strictly, and neither rule applying refuses at exit 2) is authored in HAND-Rust beside the discovery walk it wraps, and a selection is policy rather than plumbing, so it owes a .dag authority that the walk alone did not. It exists because discovery cannot answer for an executor handed an immutable source snapshot by content identity (gunbc.fabric_source_snapshot) — it panicked there, so source without a repository was unrunnable rather than unsupported. DISSOLVES WHEN the workspace root reaches the compiler as a MODELED FIELD OF THE REQUEST decided in .dag — v2.cli.compile_cli's plan naming the base the way it already names the source roots and the verb — at which point this selection is a fold over that plan and the Rust retains no rule. NOT dissolved by the discovery walk moving, by the refusal being reworded, or by Chunk F landing the roots walk without carrying the root itself: the trigger is the CAPABILITY of a request-carried root, not any artifact that would contribute to one")

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_receipt_plan_anchor: String = "docs/plans/cli-run-reconcile-defork.md#interim-workspace-root-scaffold"

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_loc_delta_measure: String = "code lines -- comments, blank lines and tests excluded -- of the declarations this scaffold binds: declared_workspace_root, declared_workspace_root_from, bind_process_workspace_root, try_resolve_process_workspace_root, bind_checkout_root, WorkspaceRootBasis and its impl, and the verb's binding in main.rs. It INCLUDES the 25 lines of the discovery walk relocated into try_resolve_process_workspace_root, which are not net-new to the seed: the measure is stated so the figure can be checked rather than trusted, because a bare count invites a reader to compare it with the rows above, whose measure is not recorded"

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_loc_delta_net: Int = 107

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_test_discriminator_declared: String = "declared_workspace_root_names_cwd_when_every_root_is_under_it"

data cli_run_workspace_root_selection_test_discriminator_escapes_cwd: String = "declared_workspace_root_refuses_a_root_that_escapes_cwd"
